That's also wonderful.  I expected it to list the maximum skills per
school for spells like the other page.

When doing a theoretical skill slot strategy for a class I list the
initial and maximum skills for every unrestricted class of both weapons
and spells.  Then I decided if one or more restricted ones might be
worth enhancing to basic after an artifact gift.  That gives the maximum
"possible" expenditure of skill slots.  For most classes the number is
well over 30 so they can't possibly enhance everything.

Then I decide on practical maxima and a reasonable sequence of
advancement.  Any class that can get to expert at dagger wants to get
there before anything but the most desirable melee weapon gets to
skilled.  I keep going until I've spent 30 slots or would need to use
crap weapons to spend more slots.  Such a plan rarely happens in a real
game but having a plan gives a goal and having a goal helps my play.


